{"i":710,"role":"assistant","text":"You can now write game code in C or C++ next to Lua and visual scripts, and the editor has Blender-style workspace tabs with the current layout kept as **Layout**. Both are pushed; Debug and Release build with 0 warnings and all 14 test suites pass.\n\n## C/C++ scripting (`bb67442`)\n\n**How you use it (like Unreal's C++ classes):**\n1. **Tools > New C++ Behaviour…**, type a name, **Create**. The editor writes `Source/<Name>.cpp` from a template and compiles it.\n2. Select an object, then **Details > Add Component > Native Script**, and pick your behaviour in the dropdown. Values you list in the behaviour show up under it as **Behaviour properties**, editable per object.\n3. Edit the `.cpp` and press **Ctrl+Alt+F11** (Tools > Compile Game Code). The new code loads automatically, even during Play.\n\n**What's included:**\n- **API:** `lsd/game.hpp` for C++ (one plain struct per behaviour with `on_start`, `on_update`, `on_hit`, overlaps and `on_event`) and `lsd/lsd_game.h` for plain C. The commands have the same names as Lua's.\n- **Mixing:** C++ can call events in Lua scripts and visual scripts, and Lua (`lsd.call`) and Call Event nodes reach C++.\n- **Packaging:** the compiled `Game.dll` ships with the package and runs on PCs without Visual Studio.\n- **Claude:** console commands `game.NewBehaviour`, `game.Compile` and `game.Behaviours` let Claude do all of this over MCP.\n\n**Tested:** a unit test runs a C++ behaviour and a C behaviour in Play, sending events to and from Lua. I also ran it end to end in the real editor: it created a behaviour, compiled it with your Visual Studio 2026, loaded it, and the behaviour spun a cube at about 90°/s.\n\n**Limits:**\n- When the code reloads, behaviours restart with fresh state.\n- A Native Script added during Play starts at the next Play or reload.\n- Some commands are still Lua-only (save games, timers, music, IK and others). [CODING.md](docs/CODING.md) lists them.\n- Not built yet: C++ functions as visual-script nodes, your own C++ components, a"}
